Analyze this method that processes and transforms a 256-byte network packet performing temporary mutations before calculating a checksum:

public byte ProcessAndChecksum(ReadOnlySpan<byte> payload) {
    byte[] tempBuffer = new byte[256];
    payload.Slice(0, 256).CopyTo(tempBuffer);

    for (int i = 0; i < tempBuffer.Length; i++) tempBuffer[i] ^= 0xFF;

    byte checksum = 0;
    foreach (var b in tempBuffer) checksum ^= b;
    return checksum;
}

Rewrite the method to eliminate the array allocation on the Heap.
MANDATORY REQUIREMENT: Declare the temporary working memory using 'stackalloc byte[256]' (or Span<byte> pointing to stackalloc) to perform local mutations strictly on the Stack.

